{"title":"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One student in a class of boys and girls is chosen to represent the class. Each student is equally likely to be chosen and the probability that a boy is chosen is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the probability that a girl is chosen. The ratio of the number of boys to the total number of boys and girls is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2dafffe23fdae1c8148630eba6cec263abae4bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }\\frac{2}{5} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } \\frac{3}{5} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"361\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the probability that a boy is chosen be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, so the probability that a girl is chosen is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fdd66831cbbb8238ab62234975610d1682bbb03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> (as the probabilities must sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22f389db5aead2a95eb92cc491894cc377ff3e3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{3}(1-p) = p &amp;\\iff 2(1-p) = 3p \\\\ &amp;\\iff 2-2p = 3p \\\\&amp;\\iff 5p = 2 \\\\&amp;\\iff p = \\frac{2}{5}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"258\" height=\"131\" />\n</p><p>Now simply notice that the probability a boy is chosen is precisely the proportion of the number of boys out of the total number of students (boys and girls), so the answer is precisely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/5388e75ace254616ec43f78cb29dafbed3c7dbc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B)} \\ \\frac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"56\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME\" title=\"1985 AHSME\">1985 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1985 AH